Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:12:13 +0200
Subject: [ARCHEOLOGY] kickpi-k2b-v2: fix 1G Ethernet packet loss (RGMII
 delays)

> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > The MAE0621A PHY driver clears the PHY-side RGMII delay bits at
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > probe. Plain "rgmii" mode then keeps only the 700 ps MAC TX delay of
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > the H618 GMAC. That is below the RGMII setup window. The 1G link
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > comes up but drops 30-100% of packets. 100M is not affected.
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > Touch the delay bits only when the phy-mode assigns them
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > (rgmii-txid/rgmii-rxid/rgmii-id). Plain "rgmii" keeps the strapped
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > PHY delay. The board DTS keeps the vendor values: rgmii,
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > tx-delay-ps 700, rx-delay-ps 2000.
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > Tested on KickPi K2B V2 (H618 + MAE0621A-Q2C), kernel 6.18.57:
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > link at 1G, DHCP lease, ping 0% loss over 200 packets both ways,
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > iperf3 TCP 310/225 Mbps, UDP 260 Mbps at 0.49% loss, jitter
> X-Git-Archeology: > recovered message: > 0.016 ms. All MAC error counters stay zero.
> X-Git-Archeology: - Revision fd2ec1ffeee4137c0aa5a8c77d9ed6a935381388: https://github.com/armbian/build/commit/fd2ec1ffeee4137c0aa5a8c77d9ed6a935381388
> X-Git-Archeology:   Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:12:13 +0200
> X-Git-Archeology:   From: Novice-PG <novice-pg@users.noreply.github.com>
> X-Git-Archeology:   Subject: kickpi-k2b-v2: fix 1G Ethernet packet loss (RGMII delays)
> X-Git-Archeology:
---
 drivers/net/phy/maxio.c | 67 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/maxio.c b/drivers/net/phy/maxio.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/maxio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/maxio.c
@@ -303,31 +303,60 @@ static int maxio_mae0621a_config_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
 	PHY_WRITE(phydev, MAXIO_PAGE_SELECT, 0x0);
 
 	/*
-	 * MAE0621A is RTL8211F-compatible. phy-mode = "rgmii" means all
-	 * RGMII delay belongs to the MAC (allwinner,tx/rx-delay-ps).
-	 * Clear PHY-side 2ns TX/RX delays if enabled by strapping, else
-	 * double delay corrupts large frames at 1G.
-	 * Same layout as RTL8211F: page 0xd08, TXCR 0x11 bit8, RXCR 0x15 bit3.
+	 * MAE0621A is RTL8211F-compatible. Page 0xd08, TXCR 0x11 bit8
+	 * and RXCR 0x15 bit3 enable a 2ns PHY-side delay each.
+	 *
+	 * Do not clear these bits when the DT does not assign delays:
+	 * the reset straps are the board's choice. The KickPi K2B V2
+	 * (H618) relies on the strapped PHY TX delay together with the
+	 * 700ps MAC delay; clearing it leaves only 700ps, below the
+	 * RGMII setup window, and the 1G link drops 30-100% of packets.
+	 * Only the RGMII_*ID phy-modes assign the delays explicitly,
+	 * so only then is each bit forced to match.
 	 */
 	{
 		int v, w;
+		bool set_delays = false;
+		u16 want_tx = 0, want_rx = 0;
 
-		v = maxio_read_paged(phydev, 0xd08, 0x11);
-		if (v < 0)
-			ret |= v;
-		else if (v & BIT(8)) {
-			w = maxio_write_paged(phydev, 0xd08, 0x11, v & ~BIT(8));
-			if (w < 0)
-				ret |= w;
+		switch (phydev->interface) {
+		case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_TXID:
+			want_tx = BIT(8);
+			set_delays = true;
+			break;
+		case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_RXID:
+			want_rx = BIT(3);
+			set_delays = true;
+			break;
+		case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_ID:
+			want_tx = BIT(8);
+			want_rx = BIT(3);
+			set_delays = true;
+			break;
+		default:
+			break;
 		}
 
-		v = maxio_read_paged(phydev, 0xd08, 0x15);
-		if (v < 0)
-			ret |= v;
-		else if (v & BIT(3)) {
-			w = maxio_write_paged(phydev, 0xd08, 0x15, v & ~BIT(3));
-			if (w < 0)
-				ret |= w;
+		if (set_delays) {
+			v = maxio_read_paged(phydev, 0xd08, 0x11);
+			if (v < 0)
+				ret |= v;
+			else if ((v & BIT(8)) != want_tx) {
+				w = maxio_write_paged(phydev, 0xd08, 0x11,
+						       (v & ~BIT(8)) | want_tx);
+				if (w < 0)
+					ret |= w;
+			}
+
+			v = maxio_read_paged(phydev, 0xd08, 0x15);
+			if (v < 0)
+				ret |= v;
+			else if ((v & BIT(3)) != want_rx) {
+				w = maxio_write_paged(phydev, 0xd08, 0x15,
+						       (v & ~BIT(3)) | want_rx);
+				if (w < 0)
+					ret |= w;
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
